    <!-- PREREQS -->
    <div class="prereq-card reveal" id="prereqs">
      <div class="prereq-card-label">Before You Begin</div>
      <h3>Prerequisites — Confirm All Before Starting</h3>
      <ul class="prereq-list">
        <li>WordPress site with admin access</li>
        <li>Gravity Forms Elite licence installed &amp; activated</li>
        <li>Gravity Forms Zoho CRM Add-On installed (Elite includes this)</li>
        <li>Access to The Building Company Zoho CRM — correct org</li>
        <li>Zoho CRM paid plan active (required for API access)</li>
        <li>Branch manager email addresses for your brand</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 1 -->
    <section class="section reveal" id="s1">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-num-block">1</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Connect Zoho CRM</h2>
          <p>One-time OAuth connection per WordPress site</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">01</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Navigate to the Zoho CRM plugin settings</div>
              <div class="step-sub">This is the plugin-level settings page — not an individual form</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <code class="nav-path">WordPress Admin <span>→</span> Forms <span>→</span> Settings <span>→</span> Zoho CRM</code>
            <p>You should see a button: <strong>"Click here to connect to Zoho CRM"</strong>. If it already says "Connected to Zoho CRM", skip to step 3.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">02</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Complete the OAuth authorisation</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Log in with The Building Company's Zoho account — not a personal account</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>Click the connect button. You will be redirected to Zoho's login page.</p>
            <div class="callout callout-warn">
              <span class="callout-icon">⚠️</span>
              <div>You must log in to the <strong>correct Zoho organisation</strong> (The Building Company). Logging in with a personal or test account will send leads to the wrong CRM. If unsure, confirm the org name with your Zoho administrator before proceeding.</div>
            </div>
            <p>Select region: <strong>zoho.com</strong>. Authorise all requested permissions. You will be redirected back to GF showing <em>"Connected to Zoho CRM."</em></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">03</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Clear the Custom Fields Cache</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Makes custom fields visible in GF feed mapping</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>On the same <strong>Settings → Zoho CRM</strong> page, scroll down and click <strong>"Clear Custom Fields Cache"</strong>.</p>
            <div class="callout callout-info">
              <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
              <div>GF caches Zoho field data for 12 hours. Clearing manually ensures your custom fields (Branch, Brand, Topic, TC Opt In) are available immediately in the feed mapping section. If they don't appear later, come back here and clear again.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 2 -->
    <section class="section reveal" id="s2">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-num-block">2</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Build the Gravity Form</h2>
          <p>Standard field structure used across all Building Company brand contact forms</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">01</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Create a new form</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <code class="nav-path">Forms <span>→</span> Add New</code>
            <p>Name it using the convention: <strong>[Brand] — [Form Type]</strong><br>Example: <code>Buco SA — Contact Us</code></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">02</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Add the standard contact fields</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Use the GF "Name" field type — it captures first and last in one field with sub-IDs</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <table class="g-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Field Label</th>
                  <th>GF Field Type</th>
                  <th>Required</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Name</td><td>Name</td><td><span class="tag tag-req">Required</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Email</td><td>Email</td><td><span class="tag tag-req">Required</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Mobile Phone</td><td>Phone</td><td><span class="tag tag-req">Required</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Branch</td><td>Drop Down</td><td><span class="tag tag-req">Required</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Message</td><td>Paragraph Text</td><td><span class="tag tag-opt">Optional</span></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="callout callout-info">
              <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
              <div>The GF <strong>Name</strong> field type stores first and last name together under one field ID, but exposes sub-IDs: <code>ID.3</code> = First Name, <code>ID.6</code> = Last Name. You'll use these in the notification message body.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 3 -->
    <section class="section reveal" id="s3">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-num-block">3</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Add Hidden Fields</h2>
          <p>Two types: static brand values and dynamic UTM campaign tracking</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">01</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Add static hidden fields — Brand and Lead Source</div>
              <div class="step-sub">These values never change — they identify which brand and form the lead came from</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>Add two <strong>Hidden</strong> field types. For each:</p>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Set the Field Label</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Go to the <strong>Advanced</strong> tab in Field Settings</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Set Default Value to the text value below</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Leave <em>"Allow field to be populated dynamically"</em> <strong>unticked</strong></li>
            </ul>
            <table class="g-table" style="margin-top:14px">
              <thead><tr><th>Field Label</th><th>Default Value</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Brand</td><td><code>Buco SA</code> &nbsp;(use your exact brand name)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Lead Source</td><td><code>Buco SA Website - Contact Us</code></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">02</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Add UTM + GCLID tracking hidden fields</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Captures Google Ads and campaign attribution data automatically from the URL</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>Add 6 more <strong>Hidden</strong> fields. For <strong>each one</strong>:</p>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Go to <strong>Advanced</strong> tab in Field Settings</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Set Default Value to <code>Parameter: [param_name]</code></li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Tick <strong>"Allow field to be populated dynamically"</strong></li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>A new <strong>Parameter Name</strong> box appears — type the exact parameter name</li>
            </ul>
            <table class="g-table" style="margin-top:14px">
              <thead><tr><th>Field Label</th><th>Parameter Name</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>utm_source</td><td><code>utm_source</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>utm_medium</td><td><code>utm_medium</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>utm_campaign</td><td><code>utm_campaign</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>utm_term</td><td><code>utm_term</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>utm_content</td><td><code>utm_content</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>gclid</td><td><code>gclid</code></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="callout callout-warn">
              <span class="callout-icon">⚠️</span>
              <div><strong>Critical:</strong> The "Allow field to be populated dynamically" checkbox must be ticked, and the Parameter Name must be filled in. Without both, UTM data will not be captured even if someone arrives from a paid campaign.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 4 -->
    <section class="section reveal" id="s4">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-num-block">4</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Configure Branch Notifications</h2>
          <p>One email notification per branch — conditional logic routes each submission to the correct manager</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">01</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Navigate to Notifications for your form</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <code class="nav-path">Forms <span>→</span> [Your Form] <span>→</span> Settings <span>→</span> Notifications <span>→</span> Add New</code>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">02</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Fill in the notification fields</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Set this up for your first branch — you'll duplicate it for all others</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <table class="g-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Name</td><td><code>Branch — [Branch Name]</code>&nbsp; e.g. <code>Branch — Alberton</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Send To</td><td>Enter Email <em>(select this radio button)</em></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Send To Email</td><td>Branch manager's email address</td></tr>
                <tr><td>From Name</td><td>Your brand name, e.g. <code>Buco SA</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>From Email</td><td><code>{admin_email}</code> <em>(leave as default)</em></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Reply To</td><td>Click <code>{...}</code> and select the Email field</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Subject</td><td><code>New Enquiry — [Brand] [Branch Name]</code></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="callout callout-info">
              <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
              <div>Setting <strong>Reply To</strong> to the customer's email field means when the branch manager hits Reply in their email client, it replies directly to the customer — not to your WordPress site email.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">03</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Write the message body</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Use GF merge tags — click {…} to browse or type field IDs directly</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>First, check your field IDs: click each field in the Form Editor and look at the <strong>Field Settings panel on the right</strong> — the ID is shown in the top-right corner of that panel.</p>
            <p>The Name field uses sub-IDs: <code>FIELD_ID.3</code> = First Name, <code>FIELD_ID.6</code> = Last Name.</p>
            <div class="code-wrap">
              <div class="code-label">Message Template — replace X with your actual field IDs</div>
              <div class="code-block">You have received a new enquiry via the [Brand] website.

Name:     {Name (First):X.3} {Name (Last):X.6}
Email:    {Email:X}
Phone:    {Mobile Phone:X}
Branch:   {Branch:X}
Message:  {Message:X}</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">04</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Enable Conditional Logic</div>
              <div class="step-sub">This is the routing mechanism — without it, every branch gets every submission</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>Scroll to the bottom of the notification. Tick <strong>"Enable conditional logic"</strong>.</p>
            <div class="code-block">Send this notification if ALL of the following match:
Branch  |  is  |  [Branch Name]</div>
            <p style="margin-top:10px">Save the notification. You should now see it listed under Notifications with an <strong>Active</strong> badge.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">05</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Duplicate for all remaining branches</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Hover over the notification in the list → Duplicate option appears</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>For each duplicate, only change these <strong>3 things</strong>:</p>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div><strong>Notification Name</strong> — update to the new branch name</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div><strong>Send To Email</strong> — update to that branch's manager email</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div><strong>Conditional Logic value</strong> — update the branch dropdown value to match</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The message body, From Name, Reply To, and Subject format all carry over from the duplicate — you only update the branch-specific parts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 5 -->
    <section class="section reveal" id="s5">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-num-block">5</div>
        <div>
          <h2>CRM Feed Mapping</h2>
          <p>Maps GF form fields to Zoho CRM lead fields — done once per form</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">01</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Create a new Zoho CRM feed</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <code class="nav-path">Form <span>→</span> Settings <span>→</span> Zoho CRM <span>→</span> Add New</code>
            <table class="g-table" style="margin-top:12px">
              <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Feed Name</td><td><code>[Brand] — [Form Type]</code>&nbsp; e.g. <code>Buco SA — Contact Us</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Action</td><td>Create a New Lead</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <p>Click <strong>Save Settings →</strong> to reveal the full field mapping section below.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">02</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Map the standard fields (top section)</div>
              <div class="step-sub">These are standard Zoho CRM fields — use the dropdown to select GF fields</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <div class="map-rows">
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Company</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Brand <em>(hidden field — shows your brand name)</em></span></div>
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Email</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Email</span></div>
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">First Name</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Name (First)</span></div>
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Last Name</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Name (Last)</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">03</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Map custom fields using Key / Value rows</div>
              <div class="step-sub">Click + to add each row. Branch, Brand, Lead_Source need the Custom Key option</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <div class="callout callout-warn">
              <span class="callout-icon">⚠️</span>
              <div><strong>Important:</strong> Custom fields like Branch, Brand, and Topic may not appear in the Key dropdown even after clearing the cache. If they don't appear, select <strong>Custom Key</strong> from the dropdown and type the field name manually. The spelling must match exactly — it is case-sensitive.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="map-rows" style="margin-top:14px">
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Phone</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Mobile Phone <em>(GF field)</em></span></div>
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Branch</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Branch <em>(GF dropdown field)</em></span></div>
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Brand</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Brand <em>(hidden field)</em></span></div>
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Lead_Source</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Lead Source <em>(hidden field)</em></span></div>
              <div class="map-row"><span class="map-key">Topic</span><span class="map-arrow">→</span><span class="map-val">Choose a Topic <em>(if form has this field)</em></span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="callout callout-info" style="margin-top:12px">
              <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
              <div>If your form has address fields (Street, City, Province, Postal Code), add them as additional Key/Value rows: <code>Street</code>, <code>City</code>, <code>State</code>, <code>Zip</code> mapped to their respective GF address sub-fields.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">04</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Map Lead Description and set Options</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>Scroll down to <strong>Lead Description</strong>. Click the <code>{...}</code> merge tag button and select your Message/Comments field. This maps the message body to the Description field in Zoho.</p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px">Under <strong>Options</strong>:</p>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Tick <strong>"Allow duplicate leads"</strong> — prevents the CRM from blocking submissions from returning customers</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Leave Approval Mode, Workflow Mode, Email Opt Out unticked</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="margin-top:10px">Leave Lead Owner, Lead Rating, Lead Source dropdown, Lead Status all as <code>-None-</code>.</p>
            <p>Click <strong>Save Settings →</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 6 -->
    <section class="section reveal" id="s6">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-num-block">6</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Test &amp; Verify</h2>
          <p>Always test before going live — check both GF entry notes and Zoho CRM</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">01</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Submit a test entry on the live form</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>Navigate to the live form page on the front-end. Fill in all fields with test data. Select a specific branch. Include a message. Use a real email address so you can verify the notification.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">02</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Check GF entry notes for errors</div>
              <div class="step-sub">This is the fastest way to catch CRM mapping errors</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <code class="nav-path">Forms <span>→</span> [Your Form] <span>→</span> Entries <span>→</span> [Test Entry] <span>→</span> scroll to Notes</code>
            <div class="callout callout-success">
              <span class="callout-icon">✅</span>
              <div><strong>Lead created. ID: [number]</strong> — CRM feed worked correctly.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="callout callout-success">
              <span class="callout-icon">✅</span>
              <div><strong>WordPress successfully passed the notification email to the sending server</strong> — branch notification sent.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="callout callout-error">
              <span class="callout-icon">✗</span>
              <div><strong>The field [X] cannot be found at Zoho CRM</strong> — custom key spelling mismatch. See Section 08 Troubleshooting.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">03</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Verify the lead in Zoho CRM</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <p>Go to <strong>Zoho CRM → Leads</strong> and find your test lead. Confirm all fields are populated:</p>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Name, Email, Phone</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Company = your brand name</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Lead Source = correct form source</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Branch = the branch selected in the form</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Brand = your brand name</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Description = the message typed</li>
              <li><div class="check-sq"></div>Layout = Website Lead Layout</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-head">
            <div class="step-dot">04</div>
            <div>
              <div class="step-title">Verify the branch notification email was received</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
