      <div class="trouble-item">
        <div class="trouble-head">
          <div class="trouble-icon">⚠️</div>
          <div class="trouble-title">The field [Branch / Brand / Topic] cannot be found at Zoho CRM</div>
        </div>
        <div class="trouble-body">
          <p><strong>Cause:</strong> The Custom Key in the GF feed doesn't match the field's API name in Zoho CRM. Field names are case-sensitive.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Go to the CRM feed, find the affected row, and check the key spelling exactly. Use <code>Branch</code> not <code>branch</code>, <code>Lead_Source</code> not <code>Lead Source</code>. If unsure, go to <strong>Zoho CRM → Setup → Leads → Fields</strong> to see the exact field label.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="trouble-item">
        <div class="trouble-head">
          <div class="trouble-icon">⚠️</div>
          <div class="trouble-title">Branch / Brand / Topic not appearing in the Key dropdown</div>
        </div>
        <div class="trouble-body">
          <p><strong>Cause:</strong> GF has cached an older version of the Zoho field list that doesn't include the custom fields.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix 1:</strong> Go to <strong>Forms → Settings → Zoho CRM → Clear Custom Fields Cache</strong>, then return to the feed.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix 2:</strong> If it still doesn't appear, select <strong>Custom Key</strong> from the dropdown and type the field name manually (e.g. <code>Branch</code>). This works identically to selecting from the dropdown.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="trouble-item">
        <div class="trouble-head">
          <div class="trouble-icon">⚠️</div>
          <div class="trouble-title">Branch and Brand are not visible on the lead record in Zoho CRM</div>
        </div>
        <div class="trouble-body">
          <p><strong>Cause:</strong> The lead was created using the Standard layout, which does not include the custom fields. The data is present but not displayed.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix (individual lead):</strong> Open the lead → click <strong>Edit</strong> → <strong>Change Layout</strong> → select <strong>Website Lead Layout</strong>.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix (all future leads):</strong> Go to <strong>Zoho CRM → Setup → Leads → Layouts → Layout Assignment</strong>. Set <strong>Website Lead Layout</strong> as the default for the Administrator profile. Save.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="trouble-item">
        <div class="trouble-head">
          <div class="trouble-icon">⚠️</div>
          <div class="trouble-title">Lead already exists — second test submission blocked</div>
        </div>
        <div class="trouble-body">
          <p><strong>Cause:</strong> You submitted a test using the same email address twice. Zoho CRM blocks duplicate leads by email address unless "Allow duplicate leads" is ticked.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix:</strong> In the CRM feed → Options → tick <strong>"Allow duplicate leads"</strong>. Or use a different email address for subsequent tests.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="trouble-item">
        <div class="trouble-head">
          <div class="trouble-icon">⚠️</div>
          <div class="trouble-title">Wrong branch manager received the notification</div>
        </div>
        <div class="trouble-body">
          <p><strong>Cause:</strong> The conditional logic value on a notification doesn't exactly match the branch dropdown option value.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Open the notification → scroll to Conditional Logic → check the branch value in the condition. It must match the dropdown option exactly, including spacing and capitalisation (e.g. <code>East London (Beacon Bay)</code> not <code>East London</code>).</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="trouble-item">
        <div class="trouble-head">
          <div class="trouble-icon">⚠️</div>
          <div class="trouble-title">Lead Description / Message not appearing in CRM</div>
        </div>
        <div class="trouble-body">
          <p><strong>Cause:</strong> The message field was mapped as a Custom Key row (<code>Description</code>) rather than using the dedicated Lead Description text area in the feed.</p>
          <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Remove the <code>Description</code> custom key row from the feed. Instead, scroll down to the <strong>Lead Description</strong> text area and click <code>{...}</code> → select the Message field. This uses the correct Zoho API endpoint for description.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>

